From: Matt
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: ocmem: go on when TZ refuses the lock

MSM8994 (OnePlus 2): qcom_scm_ocmem_lock() returns -EIO and mainline gave
up on the GPU's GMEM. Writing the GFX MPU window instead is no option
there: those registers are secure and the write resets the phone. Warn and
keep the allocation.
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/soc/qcom/ocmem.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/ocmem.c
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/ocmem.c	2026-10-27 20:31:45.665703810 +0100
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/ocmem.c	2026-10-27 20:34:36.231218389 +0100
@@ -241,11 +241,13 @@
 	if (qcom_scm_ocmem_lock_available()) {
 		ret = qcom_scm_ocmem_lock(QCOM_SCM_OCMEM_GRAPHICS_ID,
 					  buf->offset, buf->len, WIDE_MODE);
-		if (ret) {
-			dev_err(ocmem->dev, "could not lock: %d\n", ret);
-			ret = -EINVAL;
-			goto err_unlock;
-		}
+		/*
+		 * MSM8994 (OnePlus 2): TZ answers -EIO, and the GFX MPU
+		 * registers are secure there (writing them resets the phone);
+		 * go on with the range as is.
+		 */
+		if (ret)
+			dev_warn(ocmem->dev, "TZ lock refused (%d), going on unlocked\n", ret);
 	} else {
 		ocmem_write(ocmem, OCMEM_REG_GFX_MPU_START, buf->offset);
 		ocmem_write(ocmem, OCMEM_REG_GFX_MPU_END,
